WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.430
Another demonstration and another arrest for
Alexei Navalny.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.690
The years go by, but the pattern is always
the same.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:13.080
For Navalny most protests end in jail with
weeks of administrative detention.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.310
All in all he`s spent almost 5 months in jail
over the past two years.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.680
The charge - organising illegal protests.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:26.480
The only kind of protest possible in Russia,
say his supporters.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.880
And this is the work that has made Navalny
a household name in Russia – exposing what

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.129
he says are the corrupt personal fortunes
of Russia‘s leaders.

00:00:35.129 --> 00:00:39.989
In spite of a near total reporting ban on
his activities in the mainstream media.

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:44.719
This mansion, Navalny alleges, is just one
of Vladimir Putin’s private retreats.

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:48.989
WAY BEYOND the means of the president’s
officially declared earnings.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:54.269
Prime Dmitry Medvedev and what Navalny says
are his private palaces and Italian vineyard

00:00:54.269 --> 00:00:58.920
is the subject of a video that has been watched
by more than 27 million people.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.100
At a time when ordinary Russians are being
asked to tighten their belts.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.320
In public at least Russia‘s leaders have
long refused to discuss the substance of Navalny’s

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.580
allegations or even refer to him by name.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.940
But that seems to be changing.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.820
In September the head of Russias National
Guard published a video message to Navalny

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.670
online, challenging him to a duel and promising
to make “mincemeat” of him.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:26.570
This came after an investigation by Navalny’s
team alleging widespread corruption in the

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.680
way the National Guard buys food for its troops.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:34.690
The only problem – Navalny was once again
in jail at the time and unable to respond.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.840
When he is out of jail Navalny is able to
mobilise his supporters like no other leader

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.600
of the Russian opposition.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.280
Not just in Moscow but around the country.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.830
As public unrest grows over unpopular plans
to raise the pension age, that is a threat

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.500
the Kremlin seems to be taking very seriously
indeed.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:57.640
But equally the authorities seem unwilling
to lock Alexey Navalny up for any length of

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.470
time, at the risk of turning him INTO A MARTYR/PRISONER
OF CONSCIENCE.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:06.140
Instead, for now it seems like his frequent
trips to prison are set to continue – as

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:10.729
here in September, where police were waiting
to detain him as soon as he left prison on

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:11.739
another charge.

